$\lvert R_x\rvert$ and $\lvert R^{y}\rvert$ are all defined, and each is a
natural number ([[def-finite-cardinality]]).

**(b) The fibres are the slices of $R$, up to a bijection.** For $x \in X$,

$$R \cap (\{x\} \times Y) \;=\; \{x\} \times R_x ,$$

